  "label": "Anti-Latino/Hispanic Stereotypes",
  "description": "The meme relies on the stereotype that Latino/Hispanic individuals are associated with illegal immigration, criminality, and are perceived as a threat to national security. This stereotype is used to dehumanize and incite fear toward this group, portraying them as dangerous and undeserving of compassion or legal protection. The cowboy imagery reinforces a violent, punitive, and border-enforcing narrative that is rooted in historical and contemporary racialized discourse.",
